ext","value":"If the query has observers, defers to whether any observer's current\nresult reports "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isStale"},{"type":"text","value":" (which accounts for each observer's own\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"staleTime"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"enabled"},{"type":"text","value":" state)."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If the query has no observers, it is considered stale when it has no\ndata or has been invalidated."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"returns-12","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"boolean"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":" if the query is stale."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"see-2","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"#isstalebytime","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Query#isStaleByTime"}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"example-5","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"if (query.isStale()) {\n  // refetch or otherwise treat the cached data as outdated\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"isstalebytime","children":[{"type":"text","value":"isStaleByTime()"}]},{"type":"code","value":"isStaleByTime(staleTime?: number | \"static\"): boolean;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/query.ts#L561","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/query-core/src/query.ts:561"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":" if the query's data is stale relative to the given\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"staleTime"},{"type":"text","value":" (defaults to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"0"},{"type":"text","value":")."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A query with no data is always stale."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"staleTime: 'static'"},{"type":"text","value":" is never stale."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"An invalidated query is always stale."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Otherwise, staleness is based on elapsed time since "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dataUpdatedAt"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"parameters-4","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":5,"id":"staletime","children":[{"type":"text","value":"staleTime?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"},{"type":"text","value":" | "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"static\""}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The time, in milliseconds, after which data is considered stale, or\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'static'"},{"type":"text","value":" to never treat existing data as stale. A query without data is stale either way."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"returns-13","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"boolean"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":" if the query's data is stale."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"see-3","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"#isstale","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Query#isStale"}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"example-6","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const isStale = query.isStaleByTime(1000 * 60)","lang":"ts"},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"isstatic","children":[{"type":"text","value":"isStatic()"}]},{"type":"code","value":"isStatic(): boolean;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/query.ts#L506","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/query-core/src/query.ts:506"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":" if the query has at least one observer configured with\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"staleTime: 'static'"},{"type":"text","value":", meaning it is treated as never stale."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"returns-14","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"boolean"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":" if the query is static."}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"reset","children":[{"type":"text","value":"reset()"}]},{"type":"code","value":"reset(): void;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/query.ts#L459","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/query-core/src/query.ts:459"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Resets the query back to its initial state (the state it had when it was\nfirst created, e.g. any "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"initialData"},{"type":"text","value":"), destroying it first to cancel any\nin-flight fetch."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"returns-15","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"void"}]},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"setstate","children":[{"type":"text","value":"setState()"}]},{"type":"code","value":"setState(state: Partial<QueryState<TData, TError>>): void;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/query.ts#L411","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/query-core/src/query.ts:411"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Merges the given partial state directly into this query's state, notifying observers. Used\nby persistence and broadcast plugins to restore a state snapshot, and by devtools to let a\nuser manually trigger a loading/error state or edit the cached data."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"parameters-5","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":5,"id":"state-2","children":[{"type":"text","value":"state"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Partial"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/QueryState.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"QueryState"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TData"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TError"},{"type":"text","value":">>"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The partial state to merge into the query's state."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"returns-16","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"void"}]}],"headings":[{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":2},{"id":"extends","text":"Extends","level":2},{"id":"type-parameters","text":"Type Parameters","level":2},{"id":"tqueryfndata","text":"TQueryFnData","level":3},{"id":"terror","text":"TError","level":3},{"id":"tdata","text":"TData","level":3},{"id":"tquerykey","text":"TQueryKey","level":3},{"id":"constructors","text":"Constructors","level":2},{"id":"constructor","text":"Constructor","level":3},{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":4},{"id":"config","text":"config","level":5},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":4},{"id":"overrides","text":"Overrides","level":4},{"id":"properties","text":"Properties","level":2},{"id":"gctime","text":"gcTime","level":3},{"id":"inherited-from","text":"Inherited from","level":4},{"id":"observers","text":"observers","level":3},{"id":"options","text":"options","level":3},{"id":"queryhash","text":"queryHash","level":3},{"id":"querykey","text":"queryKey","level":3},{"id":"state","text":"state","level":3},{"id":"accessors","text":"Accessors","level":2},{"id":"meta","text":"meta","level":3},{"id":"get-signature","text":"Get Signature","level":4},{"id":"returns-2","text":"Returns","level":5},{"id":"promise","text":"promise","level":3},{"id":"get-signature-2","text":"Get Signature","level":4},{"id":"returns-3","text":"Returns","level":5},{"id":"methods","text":"Methods","level":2},{"id":"cancel","text":"cancel()","level":3},{"id":"parameters-2","text":"Parameters","level":4},{"id":"options-2","text":"options?","level":5},{"id":"returns-4","text":"Returns","level":4},{"id":"example-2","text":"Example","level":4},{"id":"destroy","text":"destroy()","level":3},{"id":"returns-5","text":"Returns","level":4},{"id":"see","text":"See","level":4},{"id":"overrides-2","text":"Overrides","level":4},{"id":"fetch","text":"fetch()","level":3},{"id":"parameters-3","text":"Parameters","level":4},{"id":"options-3","text":"options?","level":5},{"id":"fetchoptions","text":"fetchOptions?","level":5},{"id":"returns-6","text":"Returns","level":4},{"id":"getobserverscount","text":"getObserversCount()","level":3},{"id":"returns-7","text":"Returns","level":4},{"id":"example-3","text":"Example","level":4},{"id":"invalidate","text":"invalidate()","level":3},{"id":"returns-8","text":"Returns","level":4},{"id":"example-4","text":"Example","level":4},{"id":"isactive","text":"isActive()","level":3},{"id":"returns-9","text":"Returns","level":4},{"id":"isdisabled","text":"isDisabled()","level":3},{"id":"returns-10","text":"Returns","level":4},{"id":"isfetched","text":"isFetched()","level":3},{"id":"returns-11","text":"Returns","level":4},{"id":"isstale","text":"isStale()","level":3},{"id":"returns-12","text":"Returns","level":4},{"id":"see-2","text":"See","level":4},{"id":"example-5","text":"Example","level":4},{"id":"isstalebytime","text":"isStaleByTime()","level":3},{"id":"parameters-4","text":"Parameters","level":4},{"id":"staletime","text":"staleTime?","level":5},{"id":"returns-13","text":"Returns","level":4},{"id":"see-3","text":"See","level":4},{"id":"example-6","text":"Example","level":4},{"id":"isstatic","text":"isStatic()","level":3},{"id":"returns-14","text":"Returns","level":4},{"id":"reset","text":"reset()","level":3},{"id":"returns-15","text":"Returns","level":4},{"id":"setstate","text":"setState()","level":3},{"id":"parameters-5","text":"Parameters","level":4},{"id":"state-2","text":"state","level":5},{"id":"returns-16","text":"Returns","level":4}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nDefined in: [packages/query-core/src/query.ts:283](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/query.ts#L283)\n\nRepresents a single cached query. A `Query` holds the query's key, options,\nstate (data/error/status), and the observers currently subscribed to it.\n\nInstances are created and managed internally by `QueryCache`; application\ncode typically interacts with queries indirectly through `QueryClient` or\na framework hook like `useQuery`. Direct access to a `Query` instance is\npossible via `queryCache.find()`/`findAll()` for inspecting cache state.\n\n## Example\n\n```ts\nconst queryCache = queryClient.getQueryCache()\nconst query = queryCache.find({ queryKey: ['posts'] })\n\nif (query) {\n  console.log(query.state.dataUpdatedAt)\n}\n```\n\n## Extends\n\n- `Removable`\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TQueryFnData\n\n`TQueryFnData` = `unknown`\n\n### TError\n\n`TError` = [`DefaultError`](../type-aliases/DefaultError.md)\n\n### TData\n\n`TData` = `TQueryFnData`\n\n### TQueryKey\n\n`TQueryKey` *extends* [`QueryKey`](../type-aliases/QueryKey.md) = [`QueryKey`](../type-aliases/QueryKey.md)\n\n## Constructors\n\n### Constructor\n\n```ts\nnew Query<TQueryFnData, TError, TData, TQueryKey>(config: QueryConfig<TQueryFnData, TError, TData, TQueryKey>): Query<TQueryFnData, TError, TData, TQueryKey>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/query-core/src/query.ts:304](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/query.ts#L304)\n\n#### Parameters\n\n##### config\n\n`QueryConfig`\\<`TQueryFnData`, `TError`, `TData`, `TQueryKey`\\>\n\n#### Returns\n\n`Query`\\<`TQueryFnData`, `TError`, `TData`, `TQueryKey`\\>\n\n#### Overrides\n\n```ts\nRemovable.constructor\n```\n\n## Properties\n\n### gcTime\n\n```ts\ngcTime: number;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/query-core/src/removable.ts:11](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/removable.ts#L11)\n\n#### Inherited from\n\n```ts\nRemovable.gcTime\n```\n\n***\n\n### observers\n\n```ts\nobservers: QueryObserver<any, any, any, any, any>[];\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/query-core/src/query.ts:300](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/query.ts#L300)\n\n***\n\n### options\n\n```ts\noptions: QueryOptions<TQueryFnData, TError, TData, TQueryKey>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/query-core/src/query.ts:291](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/query.ts#L291)\n\n***\n\n### queryHash\n\n```ts\nqueryHash: string;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/query-core/src/query.ts:290](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/query.ts#L290)\n\n***\n\n### queryKey\n\n```ts\nqueryKey: TQueryKey;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/query-core/src/query.ts:289](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/query.ts#L289)\n\n***\n\n### state\n\n```ts\nstate: QueryState<TData, TError>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/query-core/src/query.ts:292](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/query.ts#L292)\n\n## Accessors\n\n### meta\n\n#### Get Signature\n\n```ts\nget meta(): Record<string, unknown> | undefined;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/query-core/src/query.ts:323](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/query.ts#L323)\n\nThe `meta` object passed in the query's options, if any.\n\n##### Returns\n\n`Record`\\<`string`, `unknown`\\> \\| `undefined`\n\nThe query's `meta`, or `undefined` if none was set.\n\n***\n\n### promise\n\n#### Get Signature\n\n```ts\nget promise(): Promise<TData> | undefined;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/query-core/src/query.ts:341](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/query.ts#L341)\n\nThe promise for the currently in-flight fetch, if the query is fetching.\n`undefined` when the query is not fetching.\n\n##### Returns\n\n`Promise`\\<`TData`\\> \\| `undefined`\n\nThe promise of the in-flight fetch, or `undefined`.\n\n## Methods\n\n### cancel()\n\n```ts\ncancel(options?: CancelOptions): Promise<void>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/query-core/src/query.ts:427](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/query.ts#L427)\n\nCancels the query's currently in-flight fetch, if any.\n- Returns a promise that resolves once the cancellation has settled.\n- If no fetch is in progress, resolves immediately.\n\n#### Parameters\n\n##### options?\n\n[`CancelOptions`](../interfaces/CancelOptions.md)\n\nSet `revert` to restore the state from before the fetch started, and `silent`\nto suppress the cancellation error when a new fetch replaces the cancelled one.\n\n#### Returns\n\n`Promise`\\<`void`\\>\n\nA promise that resolves once the cancellation has settled.\n\n#### Example\n\n```ts\nawait query.cancel()\n```\n\n***\n\n### destroy()\n\n```ts\ndestroy(): void;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/query-core/src/query.ts:439](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/query.ts#L439)\n\nClears the query's garbage collection timeout and silently cancels any\nin-flight fetch. Called by `QueryCache` when the query is removed from\nthe cache.\n\n#### Returns\n\n`void`\n\n#### See\n\n[Query#cancel](#cancel)\n\n#### Overrides\n\n```ts\nRemovable.destroy\n```\n\n***\n\n### fetch()\n\n```ts\nfetch(options?: QueryOptions<TQueryFnData, TError, TData, TQueryKey, never>, fetchOptions?: FetchOptions<TQueryFnData>): Promise<TData>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/query-core/src/query.ts:703](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/query.ts#L703)\n\nFetches the query, i.e. runs its `queryFn` (through any configured\nretryer/behavior) and updates the query's state with the result.\n- If a fetch is already in flight, returns its promise instead of\n  starting a new one, unless `fetchOptions.cancelRefetch` is set and the\n  query already has data, in which case the current fetch is silently\n  cancelled first.\n- If `options` is passed, it replaces the query's current options\n  before fetching.\n\n#### Parameters\n\n##### options?\n\n[`QueryOptions`](../interfaces/QueryOptions.md)\\<`TQueryFnData`, `TError`, `TData`, `TQueryKey`, `never`\\>\n\nQuery options that replace the query's current options before fetching. They\nare not applied when an in-flight fetch is reused.\n\n##### fetchOptions?\n\n`FetchOptions`\\<`TQueryFnData`\\>\n\nSet `cancelRefetch` to cancel an in-flight fetch first (only if the query\nalready has data), and `meta` to pass extra information to the query's behavior.\n\n#### Returns\n\n`Promise`\\<`TData`\\>\n\nA promise that resolves with the fetched data, or rejects with the fetch error. If the\nfetch is cancelled with `revert` while the query has data, it resolves with the restored data\ninstead.\n\n***\n\n### getObserversCount()\n\n```ts\ngetObserversCount(): number;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/query-core/src/query.ts:667](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/query.ts#L667)\n\nReturns the number of observers currently subscribed to this query.\n\n#### Returns\n\n`number`\n\nThe number of observers.\n\n#### Example\n\n```ts\nif (query.getObserversCount() === 0) {\n  // no component is currently watching this query\n}\n```\n\n***\n\n### invalidate()\n\n```ts\ninvalidate(): void;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/query-core/src/query.ts:680](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/query.ts#L680)\n\nMarks the query as invalidated, unless it is already invalidated. This\nupdates `state.isInvalidated` and notifies observers, but does not by\nitself trigger a refetch.\n\n#### Returns\n\n`void`\n\n#### Example\n\n```ts\nquery.invalidate()\n```\n\n***\n\n### isActive()\n\n```ts\nisActive(): boolean;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/query-core/src/query.ts:469](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/query.ts#L469)\n\nReturns `true` if the query has at least one observer for which `enabled`\ndoes not resolve to `false`.\n\n#### Returns\n\n`boolean`\n\n`true` if the query has an enabled observer.\n\n***\n\n### isDisabled()\n\n```ts\nisDisabled(): boolean;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/query-core/src/query.ts:484](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/query.ts#L484)\n\nReturns `true` if the query is disabled, meaning it will not fetch\nautomatically.\n- If the query has observers, it is disabled when none of them are active\n  (see `isActive`).\n- If the query has no observers, it is disabled when its `queryFn` is\n  `skipToken` or it has never been fetched.\n\n#### Returns\n\n`boolean`\n\n`true` if the query is disabled.\n\n***\n\n### isFetched()\n\n```ts\nisFetched(): boolean;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/query-core/src/query.ts:497](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/query.ts#L497)\n\nReturns `true` if the query has been fetched, i.e. it has resolved with\neither data or an error at least once.\n\n#### Returns\n\n`boolean`\n\n`true` if the query has been fetched.\n\n***\n\n### isStale()\n\n```ts\nisStale(): boolean;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/query-core/src/query.ts:533](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/query.ts#L533)\n\nReturns `true` if the query is stale.\n- If the query has observers, defers to whether any observer's current\n  result reports `isStale` (which accounts for each observer's own\n  `staleTime` and `enabled` state).\n- If the query has no observers, it is considered stale when it has no\n  data or has been invalidated.\n\n#### Returns\n\n`boolean`\n\n`true` if the query is stale.\n\n#### See\n\n[Query#isStaleByTime](#isstalebytime)\n\n#### Example\n\n```ts\nif (query.isStale()) {\n  // refetch or otherwise treat the cached data as outdated\n}\n```\n\n***\n\n### isStaleByTime()\n\n```ts\nisStaleByTime(staleTime?: number | \"static\"): boolean;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/query-core/src/query.ts:561](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/query.ts#L561)\n\nReturns `true` if the query's data is stale relative to the given\n`staleTime` (defaults to `0`).\n- A query with no data is always stale.\n- `staleTime: 'static'` is never stale.\n- An invalidated query is always stale.\n- Otherwise, staleness is based on elapsed time since `dataUpdatedAt`.\n\n#### Parameters\n\n##### staleTime?\n\n`number` \\| `\"static\"`\n\nThe time, in milliseconds, after which data is considered stale, or\n`'static'` to never treat existing data as stale. A query without data is stale either way.\n\n#### Returns\n\n`boolean`\n\n`true` if the query's data is stale.\n\n#### See\n\n[Query#isStale](#isstale)\n\n#### Example\n\n```ts\nconst isStale = query.isStaleByTime(1000 * 60)\n```\n\n***\n\n### isStatic()\n\n```ts\nisStatic(): boolean;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/query-core/src/query.ts:506](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/query.ts#L506)\n\nReturns `true` if the query has at least one observer configured with\n`staleTime: 'static'`, meaning it is treated as never stale.\n\n#### Returns\n\n`boolean`\n\n`true` if the query is static.\n\n***\n\n### reset()\n\n```ts\nreset(): void;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/query-core/src/query.ts:459](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/query.ts#L459)\n\nResets the query back to its initial state (the state it had when it was\nfirst created, e.g. any `initialData`), destroying it first to cancel any\nin-flight fetch.\n\n#### Returns\n\n`void`\n\n***\n\n### setState()\n\n```ts\nsetState(state: Partial<QueryState<TData, TError>>): void;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/query-core/src/query.ts:411](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/query.ts#L411)\n\nMerges the given partial state directly into this query's state, notifying observers. Used\nby persistence and broadcast plugins to restore a state snapshot, and by devtools to let a\nuser manually trigger a loading/error state or edit the cached data.\n\n#### Parameters\n\n##### state\n\n`Partial`\\<[`QueryState`](../interfaces/QueryState.md)\\<`TData`, `TError`\\>\\>\n\nThe partial state to merge into the query's state.\n\n#### Returns\n\n`void`\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: Query\ntitle: Query\n---\n\nDefined in: [packages/query-core/src/query.ts:283](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/query.ts#L283)\n\nRepresents a single cached query. A `Query` holds the query's key, options,\nstate (data/error/status), and the observers currently subscribed to it.\n\nInstances are created and managed internally by `QueryCache`; application\ncode typically interacts with queries indirectly through `QueryClient` or\na framework hook like `useQuery`. Direct access to a `Query` instance is\npossible via `queryCache.find()`/`findAll()` for inspecting cache state.\n\n## Example\n\n```ts\nconst queryCache = queryClient.getQueryCache()\nconst query = queryCache.find({ queryKey: ['posts'] })\n\nif (query) {\n  console.log(query.state.dataUpdatedAt)\n}\n```\n\n## Extends\n\n- `Removable`\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TQueryFnData\n\n`TQueryFnData` = `unknown`\n\n### TError\n\n`TError` = [`DefaultError`](../type-aliases/DefaultError.md)\n\n### TData\n\n`TData` = `TQueryFnData`\n\n### TQueryKey\n\n`TQueryKey` *extends* [`QueryKey`](../type-aliases/QueryKey.md) = [`QueryKey`](../type-aliases/QueryKey.md)\n\n## Constructors\n\n### Constructor\n\n```ts\nnew Query<TQueryFnData, TError, TData, TQueryKey>(config: QueryConfig<TQueryFnData, TError, TData, TQueryKey>): Query<TQueryFnData, TError, TData, TQueryKey>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/query-core/src/query.ts:304](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/query.ts#L304)\n\n#### Parameters\n\n##### config\n\n`QueryConfig`\\<`TQueryFnData`, `TError`, `TData`, `TQueryKey`\\>\n\n#### Returns\n\n`Query`\\<`TQueryFnData`, `TError`, `TData`, `TQueryKey`\\>\n\n#### Overrides\n\n```ts\nRemovable.constructor\n```\n\n## Properties\n\n### gcTime\n\n```ts\ngcTime: number;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/query-core/src/removable.ts:11](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/removable.ts#L11)\n\n#### Inherited from\n\n```ts\nRemovable.gcTime\n```\n\n***\n\n### observers\n\n```ts\nobservers: QueryObserver<any, any, any, any, any>[];\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/query-core/src/query.ts:300](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/query.ts#L300)\n\n***\n\n### options\n\n```ts\noptions: QueryOptions<TQueryFnData, TError, TData, TQueryKey>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/query-core/src/query.ts:291](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/query.ts#L291)\n\n***\n\n### queryHash\n\n```ts\nqueryHash: string;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/query-core/src/query.ts:290](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/query.ts#L290)\n\n***\n\n### queryKey\n\n```ts\nqueryKey: TQueryKey;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/query-core/src/query.ts:289](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/query.ts#L289)\n\n***\n\n### state\n\n```ts\nstate: QueryState<TData, TError>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/query-core/src/query.ts:292](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/query.ts#L292)\n\n## Accessors\n\n### meta\n\n#### Get Signature\n\n```ts\nget meta(): Record<string, unknown> | undefined;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/query-core/src/query.ts:323](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/query.ts#L323)\n\nThe `meta` object passed in the query's options, if any.\n\n##### Returns\n\n`Record`\\<`string`, `unknown`\\> \\| `undefined`\n\nThe query's `meta`, or `undefined` if none was set.\n\n***\n\n### promise\n\n#### Get Signature\n\n```ts\nget promise(): Promise<TData> | undefined;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/query-core/src/query.ts:341](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/query.ts#L341)\n\nThe promise for the currently in-flight fetch, if the query is fetching.\n`undefined` when the query is not fetching.\n\n##### Returns\n\n`Promise`\\<`TData`\\> \\| `undefined`\n\nThe promise of the in-flight fetch, or `undefined`.\n\n## Methods\n\n### cancel()\n\n```ts\ncancel(options?: CancelOptions): Promise<void>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/query-core/src/query.ts:427](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/query.ts#L427)\n\nCancels the query's currently in-flight fetch, if any.\n- Returns a promise that resolves once the cancellation has settled.\n- If no fetch is in progress, resolves immediately.\n\n#### Parameters\n\n##### options?\n\n[`CancelOptions`](../interfaces/CancelOptions.md)\n\nSet `revert` to restore the state from before the fetch started, and `silent`\nto suppress the cancellation error when a new fetch replaces the cancelled one.\n\n#### Returns\n\n`Promise`\\<`void`\\>\n\nA promise that resolves once the cancellation has settled.\n\n#### Example\n\n```ts\nawait query.cancel()\n```\n\n***\n\n### destroy()\n\n```ts\ndestroy(): void;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/query-core/src/query.ts:439](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/query.ts#L439)\n\nClears the query's garbage collection timeout and silently cancels any\nin-flight fetch. Called by `QueryCache` when the query is removed from\nthe cache.\n\n#### Returns\n\n`void`\n\n#### See\n\n[Query#cancel](#cancel)\n\n#### Overrides\n\n```ts\nRemovable.destroy\n```\n\n***\n\n### fetch()\n\n```ts\nfetch(options?: QueryOptions<TQueryFnData, TError, TData, TQueryKey, never>, fetchOptions?: FetchOptions<TQueryFnData>): Promise<TData>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/query-core/src/query.ts:703](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/query.ts#L703)\n\nFetches the query, i.e. runs its `queryFn` (through any configured\nretryer/behavior) and updates the query's state with the result.\n- If a fetch is already in flight, returns its promise instead of\n  starting a new one, unless `fetchOptions.cancelRefetch` is set and the\n  query already has data, in which case the current fetch is silently\n  cancelled first.\n- If `options` is passed, it replaces the query's current options\n  before fetching.\n\n#### Parameters\n\n##### options?\n\n[`QueryOptions`](../interfaces/QueryOptions.md)\\<`TQueryFnData`, `TError`, `TData`, `TQueryKey`, `never`\\>\n\nQuery options that replace the query's current options before fetching. They\nare not applied when an in-flight fetch is reused.\n\n##### fetchOptions?\n\n`FetchOptions`\\<`TQueryFnData`\\>\n\nSet `cancelRefetch` to cancel an in-flight fetch first (only if the query\nalready has data), and `meta` to pass extra information to the query's behavior.\n\n#### Returns\n\n`Promise`\\<`TData`\\>\n\nA promise that resolves with the fetched data, or rejects with the fetch error. If the\nfetch is cancelled with `revert` while the query has data, it resolves with the restored data\ninstead.\n\n***\n\n### getObserversCount()\n\n```ts\ngetObserversCount(): number;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/query-core/src/query.ts:667](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/query.ts#L667)\n\nReturns the number of observers currently subscribed to this query.\n\n#### Returns\n\n`number`\n\nThe number of observers.\n\n#### Example\n\n```ts\nif (query.getObserversCount() === 0) {\n  // no component is currently watching this query\n}\n```\n\n***\n\n### invalidate()\n\n```ts\ninvalidate(): void;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/query-core/src/query.ts:680](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/query.ts#L680)\n\nMarks the query as invalidated, unless it is already invalidated. This\nupdates `state.isInvalidated` and notifies observers, but does not by\nitself trigger a refetch.\n\n#### Returns\n\n`void`\n\n#### Example\n\n```ts\nquery.invalidate()\n```\n\n***\n\n### isActive()\n\n```ts\nisActive(): boolean;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/query-core/src/query.ts:469](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/query.ts#L469)\n\nReturns `true` if the query has at least one observer for which `enabled`\ndoes not resolve to `false`.\n\n#### Returns\n\n`boolean`\n\n`true` if the query has an enabled observer.\n\n***\n\n### isDisabled()\n\n```ts\nisDisabled(): boolean;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/query-core/src/query.ts:484](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/query.ts#L484)\n\nReturns `true` if the query is disabled, meaning it will not fetch\nautomatically.\n- If the query has observers, it is disabled when none of them are active\n  (see `isActive`).\n- If the query has no observers, it is disabled when its `queryFn` is\n  `skipToken` or it has never been fetched.\n\n#### Returns\n\n`boolean`\n\n`true` if the query is disabled.\n\n***\n\n### isFetched()\n\n```ts\nisFetched(): boolean;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/query-core/src/query.ts:497](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/query.ts#L497)\n\nReturns `true` if the query has been fetched, i.e. it has resolved with\neither data or an error at least once.\n\n#### Returns\n\n`boolean`\n\n`true` if the query has been fetched.\n\n***\n\n### isStale()\n\n```ts\nisStale(): boolean;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/query-core/src/query.ts:533](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/query.ts#L533)\n\nReturns `true` if the query is stale.\n- If the query has observers, defers to whether any observer's current\n  result reports `isStale` (which accounts for each observer's own\n  `staleTime` and `enabled` state).\n- If the query has no observers, it is considered stale when it has no\n  data or has been invalidated.\n\n#### Returns\n\n`boolean`\n\n`true` if the query is stale.\n\n#### See\n\n[Query#isStaleByTime](#isstalebytime)\n\n#### Example\n\n```ts\nif (query.isStale()) {\n  // refetch or otherwise treat the cached data as outdated\n}\n```\n\n***\n\n### isStaleByTime()\n\n```ts\nisStaleByTime(staleTime?: number | \"static\"): boolean;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/query-core/src/query.ts:561](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/query.ts#L561)\n\nReturns `true` if the query's data is stale relative to the given\n`staleTime` (defaults to `0`).\n- A query with no data is always stale.\n- `staleTime: 'static'` is never stale.\n- An invalidated query is always stale.\n- Otherwise, staleness is based on elapsed time since `dataUpdatedAt`.\n\n#### Parameters\n\n##### staleTime?\n\n`number` \\| `\"static\"`\n\nThe time, in milliseconds, after which data is considered stale, or\n`'static'` to never treat existing data as stale. A query without data is stale either way.\n\n#### Returns\n\n`boolean`\n\n`true` if the query's data is stale.\n\n#### See\n\n[Query#isStale](#isstale)\n\n#### Example\n\n```ts\nconst isStale = query.isStaleByTime(1000 * 60)\n```\n\n***\n\n### isStatic()\n\n```ts\nisStatic(): boolean;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/query-core/src/query.ts:506](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/query.ts#L506)\n\nReturns `true` if the query has at least one observer configured with\n`staleTime: 'static'`, meaning it is treated as never stale.\n\n#### Returns\n\n`boolean`\n\n`true` if the query is static.\n\n***\n\n### reset()\n\n```ts\nreset(): void;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/query-core/src/query.ts:459](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/query.ts#L459)\n\nResets the query back to its initial state (the state it had when it was\nfirst created, e.g. any `initialData`), destroying it first to cancel any\nin-flight fetch.\n\n#### Returns\n\n`void`\n\n***\n\n### setState()\n\n```ts\nsetState(state: Partial<QueryState<TData, TError>>): void;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/query-core/src/query.ts:411](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/query-core/src/query.ts#L411)\n\nMerges the given partial state directly into this query's state, notifying observers. Used\nby persistence and broadcast plugins to restore a state snapshot, and by devtools to let a\nuser manually trigger a loading/error state or edit the cached data.\n\n#### Parameters\n\n##### state\n\n`Partial`\\<[`QueryState`](../interfaces/QueryState.md)\\<`TData`, `TError`\\>\\>\n\nThe partial state to merge into the query's state.\n\n#### Returns\n\n`void`\n"}
